  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given two sorted arrays AAA and BBB of lengths MMM and NNN respectively. Array AAA has a total size of M+NM + NM+N, where the first MMM elements are the actual values and the remaining NNN elements are filled with zeros. Merge array BBB into array AAA such that the resulting array is sorted in non-decreasing order.\n\nNote: The merging should be done in-place in array AAA. The zeros at the end of array AAA are placeholder positions for elements from array BBB.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nFirst line contains two space-separated integers MMM and NNN - size of valid elements in array AAA and size of array BBB\nSecond line contains M+NM + NM+N space-separated integers - elements of array AAA (including trailing zeros)\nThird line contains NNN space-separated integers - elements of array BBB\n\n\nOutput Format\n\nPrint (M+N)(M + N)(M+N) space-separated integers - the merged sorted array",
    "constraints": [
      "Length of A = m+n",
      "Length of B = n",
      "0 &lt;= m",
      "n &lt;= 200",
      "1 &lt;= m + n &lt;= 200",
      "-10^9 &lt;= A[i], B[j] &lt;= 10^9"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
